  // -- bestEnding --
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.001":'None',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.002":'Fall of Shantium',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.003":'Fallen Guardian',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.004":'Occupied',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.005":'Guardian\'s Victory',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.006":'Costly Victory',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.007":'Hard-Won Victory',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.008":'Decisive Victory',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.009":'Coalition of Shantium',
  "siege_round_events_endings.bestEnding.010":'Shantium Triumphant',
  // -- epilogue --
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.001":'The last hostile banners disappear beyond the roads. The walls still stand, the gate still closes squarely, and people speak of the siege as the moment Shantium stopped being overlooked.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.002":'The siege ends with Shantium battered far less than its enemies intended. The defenses remain strong, the streets are full, and the town can look beyond survival almost immediately.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.003":'Shantium survives with its people and defenses largely intact, though nobody mistakes the result for an easy victory. Repairs, mourning, and rebuilding begin beside genuine relief.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.004":'The siege is broken, but victory is measured in patched roofs, empty beds, and names carved into fresh timber. Shantium survives because enough people decided survival was still worth the cost.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.005":'The enemy commander is defeated and the siege ends, but much of Shantium lies damaged behind you. The Guardian becomes a legend; the town must decide what to rebuild first.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.006":'The final assault meets not one isolated settlement but a web of allies. Shantium survives as the center of a new compact, independent but no longer alone.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.007":'Shantium survives under another power’s protection. The market opens again and the dead are buried, but foreign banners above the gate make survival feel complicated.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.008":'The Guardian does not return from the last battle. Yet the walls, militia, and alliances built during the siege hold. Shantium survives long enough to turn one name into a title.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.009":'The defenses fail. Fires take the roofs while survivors flee along whatever road remains open. Shantium falls—but stories of how long it resisted travel farther than its conquerors expected.',
  "siege_round_events_endings.epilogue.010":(v0,v1,v2,v3,v4,v5)=>`${v0} Final population: ${v1}. Morale: ${v2}%. ${v3}${v4}${v5}`,

